{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LsqLqRxXn73mKdVCjSKJKw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go from formal SRDs, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: SRDs define behavior -> orchestrator generates Go code in cmd/<utility>/ -> differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) compares Go binary against GNU reference binary (g-prefixed Homebrew binaries). Shared infrastructure lives in pkg/sys (syscalls), pkg/format (output formatting), pkg/testutils (diff testing), pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil.\n\n**Current state**: Generation run 44 on branch `generation-run44`. Many utilities implemented, many not started. The `requirement_states` field shows which SRD requirements are \"ready\" for stitching.\n\n**Earliest incomplete release with ready requirements**: Release 11.1 (srd097-who, R2.1-R3.3). Then release 12.0 (shred, chroot, install).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 11.1 has one remaining utility: `who` (users and pinky already implemented). srd097-who has 7 ready requirements (R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3). After 11.1, release 12.0 (srd099-shred, srd100-chroot, srd101-install) is next. With a 4-task limit: 3 tasks for who (2 impl + 1 test), 1 task to start chroot (smallest 12.0 utility at 6 requirements).\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd097-who R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1), R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd097-who R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: Test task (no SRD weight budget applies)\n\nTask 3: srd100-chroot R1.1 (w=1), R1.2 (w=1), R1.3 (w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/who implementation -- srd097-who R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml (requirements R2.1-R2.4)\n      - cmd/users/main.go (utmpx reading pattern -- users is already implemented)\n      - cmd/pinky/main.go (utmpx reading pattern -- pinky is already implemented)\n      - pkg/sys/ (system call abstractions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/who/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: who utility implementation covering R2.1-R2.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R2.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R2.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R2.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R2.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the utmpx reading pattern established in cmd/users/ and cmd/pinky/\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use os.Exit for non-zero exit codes to match GNU who behavior\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/who/main.go compiles with go build ./cmd/who/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/who/ passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All behaviors specified in srd097-who R2.1-R2.4 are implemented\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at start of main\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"cmd/who implementation -- srd097-who R3.1, R3.2, R3.3\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml (requirements R3.1-R3.3)\n      - cmd/who/main.go (existing implementation from prior task)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/who/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: extend who implementation with R3.1-R3.3 functionality\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R3.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R3.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd097-who R3.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing main.go from the prior task -- do not rewrite\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the same utmpx and output patterns already established in main.go\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/who/main.go compiles with go build ./cmd/who/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/who/ passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All behaviors specified in srd097-who R3.1-R3.3 are implemented\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"cmd/who differential tests -- srd097-who\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml (all requirements for test coverage)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-11.1.yaml (test suite specification)\n      - cmd/who/main.go (implementation under test)\n      - cmd/users/users_test.go (differential test pattern for utmpx utility)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/who/who_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests comparing who against gwho reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create TestDiff function using testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add DiffTest cases covering srd097-who R2.1-R2.4 behaviors\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add DiffTest cases covering srd097-who R3.1-R3.3 behaviors\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Skip gracefully when gwho reference binary is not i